Backport espeak_TextToPhonemesWithTerminator().

espeak_TextToPhonemes() does not tell the caller how a clause ended (full
stop, comma, question mark ...), so a caller that needs the punctuation
back -- Piper's voices are trained on phonemes with it -- cannot use the
released library. Upstream added espeak_TextToPhonemesWithTerminator() for
this after 1.52.0; this is that change, unmodified, so that libpiper links
against this espeak-ng instead of building a private copy. It has nothing
to do with QNX and goes away with the next release.

Upstream-Status: Backport (espeak-ng commit 2108b1e8, "Add espeak_TextToPhonemesWithTerminator (#2127)")

--- a/src/include/espeak-ng/speak_lib.h
+++ b/src/include/espeak-ng/speak_lib.h
@@ -544,6 +544,12 @@
 #ifdef __cplusplus
 extern "C"
 #endif
+ESPEAK_API const char *espeak_TextToPhonemesWithTerminator(const void **textptr, int textmode, int phonememode, int *terminator);
+/* Version of espeak_TextToPhonemes that also returns the clause terminator (e.g., CLAUSE_INTONATION_FULL_STOP) */
